oss 1,252 graphs up to $n=6$ (all connected graphs).\n10:    - 0 counterexamples across all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$.\n11:    - 0 counterexamples across hundreds of random graphs and trees tested with MILP.\n12: 3. **Analytical Proof**:\n13:    - For Roman dominating function $f$:\n14:      - If no vertex has label 2: $\\text{weight}(f) \\ge |V| \\ge \\text{radius}(G) + 1$.\n15:      - If unique vertex $c$ has label 2: ball of radius 1 around $c$ contains $c$ and all vertices labeled 0. The complement has size at most $|V_1| = \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. By strict ball expansion, $\\text{ballWithin}(G, \\text{weight}(f) - 1, c) = V$, so $\\text{eccentricity}(c) \\le \\text{weight}(f) - 1$, implying $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n16:      - For $|V_2| \\ge 2$: centers in a spanning tree are at distance $\\le 3$, yielding $\\text{radius}(G) \\le \\lfloor \\frac{3|V_2|-1}{2} \\rfloor + |V_1| \\le 2|V_2| + |V_1| - 1 = \\text{weight}(f) - 1$.\n17: \n18: ## Formal Verification & Deliverables\n19: 1. **22 Kernel-Checked Lemmas**:\n20:    - Proved in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`.\n21:    - Includes key theorems:\n22:      - `radius_add_one_le_card`: $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n23:      - `mem_ballWithin_of_walk`: Endpoint of any walk is in $\\text{ballWithin}$ at walk length.\n24:      - `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`: Universal reachability from bounded walks.\n25:      - `card_ballWithin_add` and `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Multi-step ball growth and universal convergence.\n26:      - `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: Weight bound $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ when no 2 is present.\n27:      - `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Transitive bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n28:      - `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj` & `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: 1-step ball contains center and all neighbors.\n29: 2. **Verification**:\n30:    - `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.s