{"step_index":1480,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:53:22Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:53:22+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:53:22+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 201 to 300\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n201: \n202: def IsTotalZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n203:   IsZeroForcingSet G S ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, ∃ w ∈ S, G.Adj v w\n204: \n205: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n206:     Decidable (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G S) := by\n207:   unfold IsTotalZeroForcingSet; infer_instance\n208: \n209: def totalZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n210:   minCard (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G)\n211: \n212: /-- `totalZeroForcingNumber` is meaningful: a total zero-forcing set exists.\n213: False whenever some vertex has no neighbour in any forcing set — isolated\n214: vertices being the common case. -/\n215: def HasTotalZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n216:   HasWitness (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G)\n217: \n218: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n219:     Decidable (HasTotalZeroForcingNumber G) := by\n220:   unfold HasTotalZeroForcingNumber; infer_instance\n221: \n222: /-- One step of reachability inside `S`: everything already in `T`, plus the\n223: vertices of `S` adjacent to it. -/\n224: def reachWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S T : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n225:   T ∪ S.filter (fun w => ∃ v ∈ T, G.Adj v w)\n226: \n227: /-- The vertices of `S` reachable from `v` without leaving `S`. Iterating `n`\n228: times suffices: each step that changes anything adds at least one vertex. -/\n229: def componentWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) (v : V) :\n230:     Finset V :=\n231:   (reachWithin G S)^[Fintype.card V] {v}\n232: \n233: /-- `S` induces a connected subgraph.\n234: \n235: The specification layer says `(G.induce ↑S).Connected`, which is a statement\n236: about walks in a subtype and carries no `Decidable` instance. This is the\n237: decidable equivalent: `S` is nonempty and every vertex of it reaches all of `S`\n238: from inside. `Connected` is `Preconnected ∧ Nonempty`, so both conjuncts are\n239: accounted for — the nonemptiness is not incidental. -/\n240: def IsConnectedSubset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n241:   S.Nonempty ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, componentWithin G S v = S\n242: \n243: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n244:     Decidable (IsConnectedSubset G S) := by\n245:   unfold IsConnectedSubset; infer_instance\n246: \n247: /-- A connected zero-forcing set: zero-forcing and inducing a connected\n248: subgraph, matching graphcalc's `is_connected_zero_forcing_set`. -/\n249: def IsConnectedZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n250:     Prop :=\n251:   IsZeroForcingSet G S ∧ IsConnectedSubset G S\n252: \n253: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n254:     Decidable (IsConnectedZeroForcingSet G S) := by\n255:   unfold IsConnectedZeroForcingSet; infer_instance\n256: \n257: def connectedZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n258:   minCard (IsConnectedZeroForcingSet G)\n259: \n260: /-- `connectedZeroForcingNumber` is meaningful: a connected zero-forcing set\n261: exists. False on every disconnected graph, which is precisely where graphcalc\n262: reports no value and where the conjectures never made a claim. -/\n263: def HasConnectedZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n264:   HasWitness (IsConnectedZeroForcingSet G)\n265: \n266: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n267:     Decidable (HasConnectedZeroForcingNumber G) := by\n268:   unfold HasConnectedZeroForcingNumber; infer_instance\n269: \n270: /- ── graph-class predicates ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n271: \n272: def IsNontrivialClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := 2 ≤ order G\n273: \n274: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) : Decidable (IsNontrivialClass G) := by\n275:   unfold IsNontrivialClass; infer_instance\n276: \n277: def IsRegularClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n278:   ∀ u v : V, G.degree u = G.degree v\n279: \n280: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n281:     Decidable (IsRegularClass G) := by unfold IsRegularClass; infer_instance\n282: \n283: def IsCubicClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n284:   ∀ v : V, G.degree v = 3\n285: \n286: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n287:     Decidable (IsCubicClass G) := by unfold IsCubicClass; infer_instance\n288: \n289: def IsSubcubicClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n290:   ∀ v : V, G.degree v ≤ 3\n291: \n292: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n293:     Decidable (IsSubcubicClass G) := by unfold IsSubcubicClass; infer_instance\n294: \n295: /-- Eulerian: connected, with every degree even (graphcalc's `eulerian` is\n296: `networkx.is_eulerian`, which requires connectivity — see GraphInvariants). -/\n297: def IsEulerianClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n298:   G.Connected ∧ ∀ v : V, G.degree v % 2 = 0\n299: \n300: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
