{"step_index":1482,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:53:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:53:24+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:53:24+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 301 to 400\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n301:     Decidable (IsEulerianClass G) := by unfold IsEulerianClass; infer_instance\n302: \n303: /-- Triangle-free: no 3-element clique. -/\n304: def IsTriangleFreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n305:   ∀ s ∈ univ.powerset, IsCliqueFinset G s → s.card ≠ 3\n306: \n307: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n308:     Decidable (IsTriangleFreeClass G) := by\n309:   unfold IsTriangleFreeClass; infer_instance\n310: \n311: /-- `K₄`-free: no 4-element clique. -/\n312: def IsK4FreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n313:   ∀ s ∈ univ.powerset, IsCliqueFinset G s → s.card ≠ 4\n314: \n315: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n316:     Decidable (IsK4FreeClass G) := by unfold IsK4FreeClass; infer_instance\n317: \n318: /-- Connected. Mathlib's `SimpleGraph.Connected` already has a `Decidable`\n319: instance on a finite vertex type (`Connectivity/Finite.lean`) and it *does*\n320: reduce in the kernel — verified directly — so this is a plain alias rather than\n321: a reimplementation. -/\n322: def IsConnectedClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop := G.Connected\n323: \n324: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n325:     Decidable (IsConnectedClass G) := by unfold IsConnectedClass; infer_instance\n326: \n327: /-- A tree: connected with `m + 1 = n`.\n328: \n329: Mathlib's `SimpleGraph.IsTree` is built on `IsAcyclic`, a statement about *all*\n330: walks, and has no `Decidable` instance — `decide` fails on it outright. The edge\n331: count is the decidable equivalent, and `isTreeClass_iff` below proves the two\n332: agree, so nothing is taken on trust. -/\n333: def IsTreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n334:   G.Connected ∧ size G + 1 = order G\n335: \n336: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n337:     Decidable (IsTreeClass G) := by unfold IsTreeClass; infer_instance\n338: \n339: omit [DecidableEq V] in\n340: /-- The computable tree test is exactly mathlib's `IsTree`. -/\n341: theorem isTreeClass_iff (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n342:     IsTreeClass G ↔ G.IsTree := by\n343:   rw [SimpleGraph.isTree_iff_connected_and_card]\n344:   simp [IsTreeClass, size, order, Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Set.toFinset_card,\n345:         SimpleGraph.edgeFinset]\n346: \n347: /-- Claw-free: no vertex has three pairwise non-adjacent neighbours.\n348: \n349: Phrased through `IsIndependentFinset` over `powersetCard 3` rather than as four\n350: plain `∀ v a b c : V` binders with `a ≠ b` side conditions: the latter is the\n351: more readable statement (and is what `GraphInvariants.lean` records) but its\n352: `Decidable` instance does not reduce, so `decide` gets stuck on it. This form\n353: reduces. -/\n354: def IsClawFreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n355:   ∀ v ∈ (univ : Finset V), ∀ s ∈ univ.powersetCard 3,\n356:     (∀ u ∈ s, G.Adj v u) → ¬ IsIndependentFinset G s\n357: \n358: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n359:     Decidable (IsClawFreeClass G) := by unfold IsClawFreeClass; infer_instance\n360: \n361: /-- Cograph: no four vertices induce a path `P₄`. -/\n362: def IsCographClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n363:   ∀ a b c d : V, G.Adj a b → G.Adj b c → G.Adj c d →\n364:     ¬ G.Adj a c → ¬ G.Adj b d → G.Adj a d\n365: \n366: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n367:     Decidable (IsCographClass G) := by unfold IsCographClass; infer_instance\n368: \n369: /- ── sub-total domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n370: \n371: /-- Sub-total domination number: least `t` whose `t` largest degrees sum to\n372: `≥ n`.\n373: \n374: graphcalc computes this by sorting the degree sequence and scanning prefixes;\n375: `largestDegreeSum` is that prefix sum expressed as a maximum over `t`-subsets\n376: (see the note there on why sorting is not available to the kernel). -/\n377: def subTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n378:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun t => Fintype.card V ≤ largestDegreeSum G t)\n379: \n380: /-- Defined exactly when *some* prefix reaches `n`. graphcalc returns no value\n381: when the scan runs off the end — an edgeless graph has every degree `0`, so no\n382: prefix ever reaches `n` — while `minUpTo` would fall back to `n`. Monotonicity\n383: of `largestDegreeSum` makes the whole-graph check `t = n` sufficient. -/\n384: def HasSubTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n385:   Fintype.card V ≤ largestDegreeSum G (Fintype.card V)\n386: \n387: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n388:     Decidable (HasSubTotalDominationNumber G) := by\n389:   unfold HasSubTotalDominationNumber; infer_instance\n390: \n391: /- ── total domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n392: \n393: /-- Every vertex has a neighbour in `s` — note `G.Adj v u` excludes `v = u`, so\n394: a vertex may not dominate itself. -/\n395: def IsTotalDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n396:     Prop := ∀ v : V, ∃ u ∈ s, G.Adj v u\n397: \n398: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n399:     Decidable (IsTotalDominatingSet G s) := by\n400:   unfold IsTotalDominatingSet; infer_instance\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
